keleton mob 'ln with  electric arrows I would recommend  leaping off your horse and slowing down  time in order to take this sucker out if  you don't he can be a pain in the ass  the fifth floor is the boss floor the  stall Knox isn't too bad use stasis on  him and aim for the eye if you've made  it this far in the trials he should be a  walk in the park  once you slay him make sure to grab the  great frost blade the flame spear and  the Thunder sword these will make your  life much easier moving forward next up  is a rest area but before you do  anything else sneak over and grab the  ferry now open up the chests and make  sure to equip the flame breaker boots  you should also get your first set of  ancient arrows as tempting as it may be  to use these let's hold on to them for  now cook some food smash some boxes and  when you ready step on to the  teleportation pad things are about to  start heating up if you have the flame  breaker boots equipped the heat won't be  much of an issue and again these first  few floors aren't too difficult  the lizalfos can be annoying but one  strike from the great frost blade should  put them out of commission  on floor 9 you'll come across a few  lizalfos and a fire wizzrobe use your  frost grade sword to kill them in one  hit and make sure to grab the meteor rod  from the wizzrobe once again let's hold  on to this guy for now next important  thing you want to hit is on floor 10  after you've cleared out the enemies  pull out mag Nice's and fish out this  chest that should net you three more  ancient arrows now the second boss is a  little more tough but if you're great  frost blade is still in good shape you  shouldn't have much trouble use the  frost blade to cool off the Beast  climates back and Hackett's exposed or  with a sword rinse and repeat until the  talus is dead now don't move there are  two fairies in this room crouch and  sneak up to them after that I'd  recommend cooking up some heat-resistant  meals but you know the drill by now  once you're ready to hit the teleporter  equip your flame spear now as long as  you have the flame spear equipped you  shouldn't have to worry about the cold  but I would use it sparingly not only  will this protect you against the cold  but it also kills lizalfos and Wiz robes  in one hit once again these first few  floors aren't too demanding something  else to note is that on the 13th floor  there is a cooking pot and the boxes  next to it have some meat I would  recommend cooking that meat before  heading out and gathering some firewood  throughout these next few floors you'll  find ice blocks that obscure treasure  chests there are a couple ways to melt  these without burning through too many  resources you can one start a campfire  near them or two you can hold a fire  arrow over them it may take a while but  the reward is well worth it especially  on the 14th floor melting the block to  the right of the start yields three more  Guardian arrows trust me you'll need  these  time for the boss floor hopefully you  still have the flame spear the meteor  rod or enough fire arrows to deal with  the ice talus follow the same strategy  as before and you should be on your way  to the safe room wait nope never mind  King Lionel if you're feeling confident  you can take them on if you want as gear  but I don't like to mess with this guy  so I typically send him into another  dimension with the help of an ancient  arrow  adios bag safe room take your time to  refuel because the real challenge is  about to begin if you don't know how to  deflect a guardian beam now's the time  to learn lock onto the Guardian hold  your shield up and when you hear the  final beep hit a to deflect here's the  sound one more time just in case you  missed it if you timed it right it's a  one-hit kill if you didn't well your  journey might be over the first floor of  this set puts you in the middle of a ton  of stationary Guardians only one will  activate it first but as you kill more  more will light up however you can  manually activate a guardian by hitting  it stick to the edges of the floor and  activate one at a time while using trees  as protection this is also where I burn  through most of my fairies and shields  if you get overwhelmed near the end use  a Guardian arrow or two but don't go  crazy cuz you're gonna need those the  next floor pits you against one mobile  guardian the quickest way to take care  of this guy apart from using an ancient  arrow is deflecting its attacks with  your shield after three successful  counters the machine will die and it's  on to the next floor now it's time to  take on a flying guardian hopefully you  have bomb arrows but if not there's a  chest on top of the center pillar that  has Sun try to get above the Guardian  and drop down once you're underneath it  aim for the bottom of its engines with  your bomb arrow now that the engines are  destroyed the guardian should come  falling down and it's useless it's kind  of sad to be honest  [Music]  welcome to floor 22 aka the guardian  party there's a guardian skywatcher a  guardian stalker and a guardian turret  first I'd run for cover in the castle  open the chests and target the sky  watcher use your bomb arrows to take out  the propellers and finish it off on the  ground then idler the stalker away from  the turrets line-of-sight and deflect it  to beam three times finally sink some  arrows into the eye of the turret or if  you're sick of Guardians just use an  ancient arrow but make sure you have one  left after you've looted the area get  ready for the final challenge and it all  comes down to this this floor can be  overwhelming but now isn't the time to  panic you're looking at about nine book  hablas on horseback  a guardian turret and of course a Lionel  let's deal with the lionel first  equipment ancient arrow and send him to  space next up let's deal with the book  goblins but you'll need to get some air  in order to avoid the Guardian turret  set some grass on fire and take to the  skies start picking off the book  hobbling while keeping your distance  from the turret after that finish off  the turret and let out a huge sigh of  relief try it with me now and that's it  you've made it to the very end it's time  to pat yourself on the back and test out  your supercharged Master Sword if you  want to see that baby in action head on  over to our YouTube channel and for more  on Zelda consider subscribing it really  helps us out thank you  [Music]
 

